# Teaching-fixture marker.
#
# Presence of this file tells scripts/verify-traceability.sh that this
# engagement is a deliberate teaching/demo fixture, not a real engagement.
#
# Effect: in --strict mode, an empty `ratified_by` is reported as a WARNING
# (and stays visible) instead of a hard FAILURE. This lets the dojo keep an
# intentionally-unratified artifact (requirements/sample/TR/TR-001.md) in the
# tree to teach the "proposed / not yet ratified" state, while still allowing
# the repo's own `verify.sh --check` gate to stay green.
#
# Real engagements MUST NOT carry this marker — they are held to the full
# strict bar (empty ratified_by => failure).
